                'Vesting taxes paid is cash the company paid for employees\' taxes on vesting shares. Diluted shares is the weighted average.', \
                'The 12-month row is the latest fiscal year, plus the year-to-date period since, less the same period a year earlier.', \
                '"n/a" means the filings have no tagged figure. History starts about 2009.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '## Notes on the Data', \
                '', \
                '- Diluted share count: no annual change is shown (share count missing for the first or last year).' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '- The cost line cannot be built from the filing tags, so the costs sign is missing and the company has no score.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '- No insider transactions in the SEC data sets for the five years, so the insiders sign is missing and the company has no score. Foreign companies have not had to file them.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '- The latest fiscal year stands in for the latest 12 months, because the quarterly data is unusable or there is no later quarter.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            ['- No capital spending tag in at least one year; that year counts capital spending as zero.'] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '---', \
                '', \
                'Data as of 2026-11-05, from SEC filings. Method version 1.1.0.', \
                'History starts about 2009, when the SEC began collecting financial statements as data.', \
                '', \
                'The index ranks how outside owners have been treated. It is not a short list, a price forecast or investment advice,', \
                'and it makes no finding about any one company\'s intent.' \
            ] \
        ] \
    ])
endfunction
unittestRunTest('testMain_companyNoCostLine')


