# An excluded industry
async function testMain_companyExcluded():
    data = testData(['data/meta.json', 'data/company/5.json'])
    systemGlobalSet('vPage', 'company')
    systemGlobalSet('vCik', 5)
    unittestMockAll(data)
    tiMain()
    log = unittestMockEnd()
    systemGlobalSet('vPage', null)
    systemGlobalSet('vCik', null)
    unittestDeepEqual(log, [ \
        [ \
            'systemFetch', \
            [ \
                ['data/meta.json', 'data/company/5.json'] \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '[Index](#var=&_top) | [Group Totals](#var.vPage=\'totals\'&_top) | [Methodology](#var.vPage=\'method\'&_top) | [Data and Limits](#var.vPage=\'data\'&_top)' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'documentSetTitle', \
            ['Bank Co - The Treadmill Index'] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '# Bank Co', \
                '', \
                '**Ticker:** BANK (NYSE) \\\n**SEC filings:** [CIK 5](https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=5&type=10-K) \\\n**Industry:** National Commercial Banks ([SIC 6021](#var.vSic=6021&var.vType=\'all\'&_top)) \\\n**Type:** Excluded industry. A bank, insurer, lender, broker, asset manager, REIT or drug developer. This company is classed as a bank.', \
                '', \
                'From fiscal 2019 to 2025, Bank Co reported $10.2 billion of revenue and $1.0 billion of free cash flow. Stock pay was $2.0 billion, which leaves -$1.0 billion of owner cash: -10.0% of revenue. Owner cash was under 3.0% of revenue in 7 of 7 years. In the 12 months to 2026-09-30 it was -10.0% of revenue.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '**Not scored.** The index leaves this industry out, because its cash flows include customer money, loans, property', \
                'or research spending that make free cash flow mean something different. The figures below are for reference only.' \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            ['', '## Insiders, 2021‑2025', ''] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                'Officers and directors who reported transactions: 1, of whom 1 took cash out.', \
                'Together they took $1.2M out through stock. They were granted stock worth $0 and options over shares worth $0 at the time.', \
                '', \
                [ \
                    '| Year | Cash taken out | Sold on the open market | Withheld for taxes or sold to the company | Paid to buy shares or exercise options | Stock granted | Options granted, at the price of the shares |', \
                    '| :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |', \
                    '| 2021 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |', \
                    '| 2022 | $1.2M | $1.2M | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |', \
                    '| 2023 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |', \
                    '| 2024 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |', \
                    '| 2025 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |', \
                    '| **2021‑2025** | $1.2M | $1.2M | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |' \
                ] \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
            'markdownPrint', \
            [ \
                '', \
                '**Who took out the most.** Select a name to list that person\'s filings.', \
                '', \
                [ \
                    '| Insider | Latest title | Cash taken out | Sold on the open market | Withheld for taxes or sold to the company | Paid to buy shares or exercise options | Stock granted | Options granted, at the price of the shares |', \
                    '| :-- | :-- | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: | --: |', \
                    '| [Doe Jane](#var.vCik=5&var.vPage=\'company\'&var.vPerson=1001&filings-of-the-selected-insider) | Chief Executive Officer | $1.2M | $1.2M | $0 | $0 | $0 | $0 |' \
                ] \
            ] \
        ], \
        [ \
